# Commit precheck

Before creating a commit, check every path the commit would add. That includes source, docs, tests, shaders, data, images, and any other file. A clean subset does not excuse an unchecked path.

## Personal data

Look for names, email addresses, phone numbers, account handles, home directories, hostnames, serial numbers, local network addresses, tokens, keys, passwords, and private URLs. Logs, screenshots, and sample output count.

Placeholders are `~/.favlo`, `127.0.0.1`, and `example-model`. The copyright line already in the repository stays. A new name does not.

When a path contains personal data, leave it out of the commit. Name the path and the kind. Do not copy the value into the commit message or the reply.

## NSFW, violent, and racist content

Look for sexual, erotic, nude, obscene, violent, racist, hateful, or abusive text, prompts, and images, including instructions to harm a person or an animal. A refusal policy may name the categories it refuses. A test may quote a request only to assert that the refusal leaves it out of the reply.

When a path contains that content, leave it out of the commit. Name the path. Do not quote the content.
